-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/5bb73161-324e-532f-aac8-9e5d42bfcdd8
-- title:
--   Cusp cancellation for the truncated twisted class sum
-- statement:
--   The setting is a Galois extension $L/K$ of number fields, with $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in `Subgroup.zpowers σ` (hypothesis `hgen`: the Galois group is generated by $\sigma$).
--
--   *Measure and character data.* The unit group $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ of the adele ring of $L$ carries a measurable structure which is the Borel structure, and $\nu_{Z_L}$ is a Haar measure on it; $\Omega_L$ is a set which, by `hΩL`, is a fundamental domain for the action of the range of $L^\times \to (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ (the principal ideles) on $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ with respect to $\nu_{Z_L}$. The datum $D$ is an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent (𝓞 L) K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28), i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which is compatible with $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$ and continuous in each element; [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14) denotes the induced automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, written $g \mapsto {}^\sigma g$ below. Further, $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top \le (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, such that $z \mapsto \xi_L(z)$ is continuous as a $\mathbb{C}$-valued function (`hξc`) and $\xi_L$ is trivial on the principal ideles (`hξt`).
--
--   *The regular diagonal element and its twisted class data.* The element $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ has vanishing off-diagonal entries (`hδ₀u`, `hδ₀l`: the $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries are $0$), and satisfies the regularity condition `hreg`: $N_{L/K}(\delta_{0,00}/\delta_{0,11}) \neq 1$. The set $I \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ is characterised by `hI` as consisting of those $\delta$ for which there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with $\delta_0^{-1}\,(g^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(g))$ central, i.e. the $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy class of $\delta_0$ modulo the centre; $I$ does not occur in the conclusion. The subgroup $\Lambda \le \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ is characterised by `hΛ` as consisting of those $\gamma$ with $\delta_0^{-1}\,(\gamma\,\delta_0\,\sigma(\gamma)^{-1})$ central (the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta_0$ modulo the centre), and $r : \iota \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, with $\iota$ countable, is a system of representatives for the left cosets of $\Lambda$: by `hr`, every $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ satisfies $(r_i)^{-1}\gamma \in \Lambda$ for exactly one $i$.
--
--   *The band and the fundamental domain.* Reals $\alpha < \beta$ with $0 < \alpha$ cut out the band $\{g : \|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}_L} \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$, where $\|\cdot\|_{\mathbb{A}_L}$ is [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19), the module of the idele acting on $\mathbb{A}_L$. Reals $c, u, d_1, d_2$ with $0 < c$ and a compact set $T_c \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ are given, and $\Phi_0 \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ satisfies three conditions: (`hΦ₀S`) $\Phi_0$ is contained in the union over $y \in T_c$ of the right translates $(\cdot\, y)$ of the centre-cut Siegel set `WindowedSiegel.centreCutSiegelSet L c u d₁ d₂`, namely the set of $g$ whose finite part lies in the full integral subgroup `finiteIntegralGL2`, whose archimedean components $g_w$ satisfy $c \le |\det g_w|/\mathrm{rowNormSq}(g_w)$ and $\mathrm{xWindowSq}(g_w) \le u^2$ at every infinite place $w$, and with $\|\det g_w\| \in [d_1,d_2]$ at every infinite place; (`hΦ₀s`) $\Phi_0$ lies in the band; (`hΦ₀`) $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the action of the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under [`AutomorphicForm.globalPoints`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L15) (written $\iota$ below) with respect to the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` restricted to the band.
--
--   *Diagonal coset data.* The subgroup $\Lambda' \le \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ is characterised by `hΛ'` as consisting of those $a$ with vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries and with $a_{00}/a_{11}$ in the image of $K \to L$; $ra : \kappa \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, with $\kappa$ countable, has all $ra_j$ with vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries (`hrad`), and by `hra` every $a \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries satisfies $(ra_j)^{-1}a \in \Lambda'$ for exactly one $j$.
--
--   *Test function.* Finally $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ is a factorizable test function in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.IsFactorizableTestFn`](def/AutomorphicForm_FactorizableTestFn.html#L38): $\varphi(g) = f_\infty(\mathrm{glArch}\,g)\, f_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathrm{glFin}\,g)$ for some $f_\infty$ of the form $\Phi \circ \mathrm{archEntries}$ with $\Phi$ smooth ($C^\infty$ over $\mathbb{R}$) on $2\times 2$ matrices over the mixed space of $L$ and with $f_\infty$ of compact support, and some locally constant $f_{\mathrm{fin}}$ of compact support on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{L,\mathrm{fin}})$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists $R_0 \in \mathbb{R}$ such that for every real $R \ge R_0$ the function $D_R$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ described next is integrable on $\Phi_0$ with respect to `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` (first conjunct), and $\int_{\Phi_0} D_R \, d(\mathrm{adelicGLHaar}) = 0$ (second conjunct).
--
--   The function $D_R$ is the difference of two terms. Writing $\iota$ for `globalPoints`, $H$ for the adelic height [`NumberField.AdelicHeight.adelicHeight L`](def/NumberField_AdelicHeight.html#L158) (the product over infinite places $w$ of $(|\det g_w|/\mathrm{rowNormSq}(g_w))^{\mathrm{mult}(w)}$ times the finite product of the local finite heights of the finite components), $w_0 =$ [`AutomorphicForm.adelicWeyl`](def/AutomorphicForm_WeylIntertwining.html#L35) (the image under $\iota$ of the antidiagonal matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$), $u(s) =$ [`AutomorphicForm.unipotentGL2 s`](def/AutomorphicForm_ConstantTerm.html#L17) $= \begin{pmatrix}1&s\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ and $z$ also for the central scalar matrix `centralScalar (𝓞 L) L z`, the first term is
--   $$\sum_{i}\Bigl(\mathbf 1[e^R < H(y_i)] + \mathbf 1[e^R < H(w_0\, y_i)]\Bigr)\,\int_{(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times} \xi_L(z)\,\varphi\bigl(y_i^{-1}\,\iota(\delta_0)\,{}^\sigma(z\,y_i)\bigr)\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z),$$
--   an unconditional sum (`tsum`) over $i \in \iota$, where $y_i = \iota(r_i)^{-1}x$; the two indicators are those of the sets $\{y : e^R < H(y)\}$ and $\{y : e^R < H(w_0 y)\}$ evaluated at $y_i$, with value $1 \in \mathbb{C}$.
--
--   The second term is
--   $$\mathbf 1[e^R < H(x)]\cdot \varepsilon \cdot V^{-1}\sum_{j}\Bigl(A_j(x) + B_j(x)\Bigr),$$
--   where $\varepsilon = 1/2$ if $N_{L/K}(\delta_{0,00}/\delta_{0,11}) = -1$ and $\varepsilon = 1$ otherwise, $V$ is the real number `(adelicAddHaar (𝓞 L) L (adelicBox L)).toReal`, the additive Haar volume of the adelic box (the preimage of the fundamental domain of the lattice basis of the mixed embedding at the infinite part, together with the integral finite adeles at the finite part), the sum over $j \in \kappa$ is again a `tsum`, and, with $y_j = \iota(ra_j)^{-1}x$,
--   $$A_j(x) = \int_{\mathbb{A}_L}\int_{(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times} \xi_L(z)\,\varphi\bigl((u(s)y_j)^{-1}\,\iota(\delta_0)\,{}^\sigma(z\,u(s)y_j)\bigr)\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z)\,d(\mathrm{adelicAddHaar})(s),$$
--   $$B_j(x) = \int_{\mathbb{A}_L}\int_{(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times} \xi_L(z)\,\varphi\bigl((w_0^{-1}u(s)y_j)^{-1}\,\iota(\delta_0)\,{}^\sigma(z\,w_0^{-1}u(s)y_j)\bigr)\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z)\,d(\mathrm{adelicAddHaar})(s).$$
--   All integrals in $z$ are over the whole group $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ against $\nu_{Z_L}$, and those in $s$ over $\mathbb{A}_L$ against the additive Haar measure `adelicAddHaar (𝓞 L) L`.
--
--   This is the cusp-decay step in the derivation of the twisted ($\sigma$-) trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension: high in the cusp, the truncated sum of twisted orbital integrals over the coset space of the twisted centraliser of a regular diagonal $\delta_0$ differs from its unfolded constant term only by a Poisson-summation discrepancy along the unipotent radical, and this discrepancy integrates to zero over the fundamental domain. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_setIntegral_finsum_sigmaConjClassOrbit_sub_indicator_constantTerm_eq_setIntegral_tsum_weight_mul_integral_of_isFactorizableTestFn`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_setIntegral_finsum_sigmaConjClassOrbit_sub_indicator_constantTerm_eq_setIntegral_tsum_weight_mul_integral_of_isFactorizableTestFn), where the class sum over the band is thereby replaced by the weighted orbital-integral expression.
